  "description": "Stereo-EEG recordings from one drug-resistant epilepsy patient with electrodes covering a right posterior temporal periventricular nodular heterotopia (PVNH) and adjacent cortex. 43 Hz electrical stimulation of the PVNH elicited autoscopic hallucinations, and single-pulse electrical stimulation was used to map effective connectivity of the underlying network. The dataset includes high-frequency stimulation and SPES recordings, event markers, contact coordinates and a defaced T1 image.",
  "methods_description": "SEEG was recorded at 4096 Hz with 148 channels (131 SEEG contacts, DC inputs, trigger and monitor channels) during 43 Hz stimulation trains and single-pulse stimulation. Original AnyWave ADES float32 data were copied unchanged into BrainVision format, with markers, bad channels, contact coordinates in FreeSurfer surface RAS and a defaced T1 converted to BIDS.",
